<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">North Caucasus</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The North <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caucasus">Caucasus</a> is the region on the northern slopes of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greater-caucasus">Greater Caucasus</a> range, between the Black and Caspian seas, home to peoples such as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chechens">Chechens</a>, Ingush, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ossetians">Ossetians</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/circassians">Circassians</a> and the many peoples of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dagestan">Dagestan</a>. It was the home of the medieval Alans and was conquered by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> in the 19th-century <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caucasian-war">Caucasian War</a>. After 1917 its peoples briefly formed their own republics.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/north-caucasus.jpg" alt="North Caucasus" width="320" height="255" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Relahs · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Map_of_North_Caucasus.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
